  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If Ivy, Gleeful Spellthief isn't a legal target for the spell, no copy can be created.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell has multiple targets but all of them are the same creature, Ivy, Gleeful Spellthief's second ability will trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the spell that's copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast, the copy has the same value of X.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the spell that's copied is modal (that is, it says \"Choose one —\" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. You can't choose a different one.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The controller of a copy can't choose to pay any additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy too. Notably, if the spell you copy was kicked, the copies will also be kicked.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The copy is created even if the spell that caused the ability to trigger has been countered by the time the ability resolves. The copy resolves before the original spell.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The copy that Ivy, Gleeful Spellthief's second ability creates is created on the stack, so it's not \"cast.\" Other abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The second ability triggers whenever a player casts a spell that targets only one creature and no other object or player. It doesn't matter who controls the creature.",
      "oracle_id": "55ad6a6b-1c44-4397-86ae-dd9221892b22",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won’t return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura’s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn’t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent’s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura’s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can’t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it’s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners’ graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may choose the same creature for both targets since the card says \"target creature\" multiple times. You may also choose two different creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "e8aa12f8-8922-41ed-8cdb-219c9e4b9e36",
      "published_at": "2013-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
